---
import Base from "../../../layouts/dc/Base.astro";
import { COMPANY, CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME, LEGAL_URL } from "../../../config/dc/product";
import { root } from "../../../lib/dc/url";
import { u } from "../../../lib/dc/url";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — DC Sim"
  description="This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and has no forms. Downloads are static files. Email us and we use your address only to reply."
  path="legal/privacy/"
  crumbs={[{ name: "Privacy", path: "legal/privacy/" }]}
>
  <article class="container page prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="direct-answer">The DC Sim pages set no cookies and run no analytics or tracking scripts. The template and example files are plain downloads that do not ask for your e-mail. The one form on the site is the waitlist, described in the <a href={root("privacy/")}>site-wide privacy notice</a>.</p>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>DC Sim is a {COMPANY} product. {COMPANY} is a brand of <a href={LEGAL_URL}>{LEGAL_NAME}</a> (Malta), which is responsible for this site and for the data described here.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served as static files by Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare receives your IP address to deliver and protect the pages, under its own privacy policy. We do not receive or use those logs.</p>
    <h2>E-mail</h2>
    <p>If you write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, {LEGAL_NAME} uses your address and message only to reply and to follow up on what you asked for. Ask us to delete the correspondence at any time.</p>
    <h2>Waitlist and "I want this"</h2>
    <p>The "I want this" buttons on planned integrations open the site's waitlist form with the integration's name in the link. What it stores and for how long is in the <a href={root("privacy/")}>site-wide privacy notice</a>.</p>
    <h2>Files you send us</h2>
    <p>If you send a filled template for a walkthrough, we import it only to show you your room, and delete it on request. See <a href={u("security/")}>security and data</a> for how the product handles customer data.</p>
    <p class="small muted">Last updated: 15 October 2026</p>
  </article>
</Base>
